id: pm-swarm-write-free-reads
title: Require write-free SDK current reads for cold refusal invariance
description: "Pinned SDK 2026.10.23 PmClient.get records derived context usage for current reads; full current gets and listAllComplete can materialize metadata caches. PmClientOptions, GetOptions and PmCompleteListOptions expose no per-call no-write mode. Public createMutationGuardSdk.get provides a pure local metadata lookup and is used for package admission, but its list method uses the persistent cache. Cold corpus-dependent or provider-owned refusals cannot yet promise zero SDK runtime writes without a write-free certified-list/current-read capability. Preserve SDK-owned caches and usage records; do not disable configuration or reimplement tracker listing. Orchestrator to report the missing SDK capability upstream."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: privacy,sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-25T10:11:49.433Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:03:45.908Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-swarm-y972
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T11:01:33.162Z",codex-agent,"Measured cold strict-overlap refusal with pinned SDK 2026.10.23: item and history bytes unchanged; zero package runtime files left; five SDK metadata-cache files created. Whole tracker byte identity is therefore false on this cold corpus read. test/sdk-read-effects.acceptance.ts generates this measurement with real SDK operations and accepts future zero-write SDK behavior. PmCompleteListOptions currently exposes includeBody only, without a non-persisting complete-list mode; preserve SDK-owned files rather than deleting peer state."
